{
  "id": "KY-HB-574-2021",
  "scope": "state:ky",
  "title": "HB 574 (2021 Regular Session (Acts ch. 197)) — Omnibus elections act (early voting, mail-in absentee, etc.); also re-enacts the proof-of-identification definition as KRS 117.001 (renumbered from 117.375) and carries ID rules forward",
  "urls": [
    "https://apps.legislature.ky.gov/record/21rs/hb574.html",
    "https://apps.legislature.ky.gov/law/acts/21rs/documents/0197.pdf",
    "https://apps.legislature.ky.gov/record/21rs/hb574/vote_history.pdf"
  ],
  "version": "enrolled",
  "operative_text": "Sec 41 (KRS 117.375 repealed, reenacted, renumbered as KRS 117.001) definition: \"Proof of identification\" means a document that was issued by:\nSec 28/30/31 in-person ID rules (KRS 117.225, .227, .228): shall provide proof of identification as defined in Section 41 of this Act\nSec 11 (KRS 117.085) in-person absentee and mail-in application: the voter shall provide a copy of his or her proof of identification, as defined in Section 41 of this Act[KRS 117.375], or the executed voter affirmation as described in KRS 117.228(1)(c).\nSections 1-87 other parts: 87 sections amend KRS chapters 83A, 116, 117, 118, 118A, 120 and create sections in chapters 48, 65, 117, 118, 120",
